## Future Scope — Extensibility

The core engine never changes. Only new Sync Writer components are added per platform.

- **WooCommerce integration** — new Sync Writer only, core engine untouched
- **Amazon Seller Central** — new Sync Writer only, core engine untouched
- **Magento** — new Sync Writer only, core engine untouched
- **Custom ERP via webhook or API** — new Sync Writer only, core engine untouched
- **Supplier portal** — suppliers upload files directly without going through the merchant
- **Custom output format per merchant** — merchant defines the exact column structure they want in the final output
- **Quantity calculation rules** — handle cases where supplier reports in_warehouse and in_transit separately and merchant wants them summed, or carton counts with a units-per-carton multiplier
- **Scheduled auto-processing** — merchant configures a supplier SFTP or email attachment source and uploads happen automatically on a schedule
- **Public developer API** — expose the core engine as a REST API so developers can integrate NormaList normalization into their own systems
- **Multi-currency price normalization** — if supplier files include pricing columns

---

## Rules That Never Change Regardless of Phase

- The core engine (Components 1 through 5) never contains platform-specific code
- Every ActiveRecord query touching merchant data must be scoped by merchant_id — no exceptions
- The mapping_dictionary is the single source of truth for all supplier-to-master mappings
- Gemini only ever receives a snippet of the file (first 10 rows), never the full payload
- platform_variant_id and platform_inventory_id in the output are always null until platform integration is explicitly built and connected
- All file processing runs in Sidekiq — never synchronously in a controller action
- All UI feedback during async processing uses Turbo Streams
- No React, No Vue — all interactivity via Hotwire (Turbo + Stimulus)
- multi-tenancy is non-negotiable — every query, every service call, every job must carry and respect merchant_id
